From: MastaG <badouri.g@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: add BC-250 VRM and GDDR6 temperature drivers

Kconfig and Makefile entries for two out-of-tree BC-250 hwmon drivers by
Liam McLoughlin (github.com/Hexxeh/bc250-vrm-dkms and bc250-memory-dkms).
The sources are fetched at their latest release tag and installed into
drivers/hwmon by the package build, the same way nct6687.c is.

- bc250_vrm: PMBus telemetry from the board's VRM controller (CPU and GPU
  rail voltage, current, temperature and power) over the AMD SMBus
  controller. Needs a small hardware modification that wires the VRM's
  SMBus lines; without it the readings fail and nothing else happens.
- bc250_memory: GDDR6 temperatures (per chip, hotspot, average) through the
  SMU. On first load it writes a small payload into SMU firmware memory and
  redirects one Queue 3 message handler (auto_patch=1, the default), which
  only works with BIOS SMU debug access enabled; with it locked the driver
  refuses to load.

Both declare a DMI match on "AMD BC-250", so udev loads them on every
board. bc250_vrm binds only when a PMBus device answers at 0x60, so it is
left to load. The package build strips bc250_memory's DMI module alias, so
it loads only when the user asks, e.g. via /etc/modules-load.d (a modprobe
blacklist would block that path too: systemd-modules-load honors it).
---
diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/Kconfig b/drivers/hwmon/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/hwmon/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/Kconfig
@@ -1782,6 +1782,34 @@
 	  This driver can also be built as a module. If so, the module
 	  will be called nct6687.
 
+config SENSORS_BC250_VRM
+	tristate "AMD BC-250 VRM telemetry"
+	depends on I2C && DMI && X86
+	help
+	  PMBus voltage, current, temperature and power readings for the CPU
+	  and GPU rails of the AMD BC-250 board's VRM controller, read over the
+	  AMD SMBus controller. Requires a hardware modification that connects
+	  the VRM's SMBus lines.
+
+	  This driver is maintained outside the upstream kernel and is
+	  integrated from https://github.com/Hexxeh/bc250-vrm-dkms.
+
+	  If built as a module, it will be called bc250_vrm.
+
+config SENSORS_BC250_MEMORY
+	tristate "AMD BC-250 GDDR6 temperatures"
+	depends on PCI && DMI && X86
+	help
+	  Per-chip, hotspot and average GDDR6 temperatures on the AMD BC-250,
+	  read through the SMU. Loading it patches SMU firmware memory to add
+	  the readout (module parameter auto_patch), which requires BIOS SMU
+	  debug access.
+
+	  This driver is maintained outside the upstream kernel and is
+	  integrated from https://github.com/Hexxeh/bc250-memory-dkms.
+
+	  If built as a module, it will be called bc250_memory.
+
 config SENSORS_NCT6694
 	tristate "Nuvoton NCT6694 Hardware Monitor support"
 	depends on MFD_NCT6694
diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/Makefile b/drivers/hwmon/Makefile
--- a/drivers/hwmon/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/Makefile
@@ -182,6 +182,8 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_SENSORS_MR75203)	+= mr75203.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SENSORS_NCT6683)	+= nct6683.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SENSORS_NCT6687)	+= nct6687.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_SENSORS_BC250_VRM)	+= bc250_vrm.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_SENSORS_BC250_MEMORY)	+= bc250_memory.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SENSORS_NCT6694)	+= nct6694-hwmon.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SENSORS_NCT6775_CORE) += nct6775-core.o
 nct6775-objs			:= nct6775-platform.o
